    {
      "id": 35587,
      "name": "Ploid",
      "slug": "ploid",
      "former_names": [],
      "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/bb8cfe58317eeba078abcb4a9b1d2c14affb42f9.png",
      "website": "https://ploid.com",
      "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA",
      "long_description": "Ploid is the AI-native people data infrastructure for building products, workflows, and agents around people. We’ve built an index of 2B+ people across professional and social sources, with the infrastructure to search, resolve, enrich, and retrieve up-to-date information about anyone on demand.\r\n\r\nThrough Ploid’s API, CLI, and MCP, developers and companies can search for people, enrich profiles, find emails and phone numbers, resolve identities across different data points, and access the broader web context associated with a person. Unlike traditional people databases that rely primarily on static records, Ploid is designed for AI-native workflows. We combine our people index with real-time retrieval and entity resolution so data can be refreshed and expanded at the moment it is requested.\r\n\r\nPloid can power everything from sales and recruiting products to customer intelligence, identity resolution, trust and safety, and AI agents that need reliable information about people. Instead of building and maintaining dozens of data integrations yourself, Ploid gives you one infrastructure layer for people data.\r\n\r\n2B+ people. One API. Built for AI.",
      "one_liner": "The people data company for the agent era",
      "team_size": 0,
